    "narrative": "Our offensive outlook for May 14th is headlined by **Will Smith**, who sits comfortably as our highest-rated starter at 65.29. Leading off against Roupp, **Will Smith** benefits from a favorable 4.07 xERA matchup and the premium run-production environment associated with the leadoff spot. Close behind is **Masyn Winn**, maintaining a solid 60.25 rating. Despite facing a left-handed arm in J. Lopez, **Masyn Winn** is buoyed by a significant park factor boost and consistent middle-of-the-order protection, reinforcing his status as a high-floor play despite the nominal platoon disadvantage. **Brendan Donovan** rounds out our top-tier plays at 59.46, thriving specifically on a 14% dynamic platoon boost that maximizes his value against Burrows, making him an essential start despite a slight park-induced penalty.\n\nNavigating the remainder of the lineup, we are exercising caution against Sheehan, whose 3.16 xERA is suppressing the scores of **Luis Arraez**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Matt Chapman**. While **Luis Arraez** maintains a 46.02 and **Jung Hoo Lee** a 47.15, both are startable only by virtue of their premium batting order positions\u2014both slated to hit 1st or 2nd\u2014which mitigates the risk posed by Sheehan\u2019s elite arm. **Gavin Sheets** sits on the fringe at 41.47; he is our most volatile asset today, hampered by a tough matchup against Harrison and a negative platoon split. Regarding our bench, **Drew Gilbert** was the closest to cracking the active roster with a 36.02, but ultimately fell beneath our 40.0 efficiency floor. The combination of an 8th-order slot and Sheehan\u2019s SP skill was too significant an anchor for his base projection to overcome, keeping him stashed as we look to protect our cumulative game caps. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Geraldo Perdomo** sidelined by an off-day, we must rely on the high-OBP skill sets of our top-of-the-order pivots to navigate this difficult slate of arms.",
